reg — Linear regression by least squares, with fixed effects        regress · tier 2 · since 0.4.0 · 1.0 · closed form

USAGE
    data.reg(formula, fe: Terms, se: classical | robust | hc2 | hc3 = classical, level: Float = 0.95)

DESCRIPTION
    Fits the outcome of `formula` on its regressors by least squares.

ARGUMENTS
    data        Frame. The data.
    formula     Formula. `y ~ x1 + x2`.
    fe:         Terms. Fixed effects absorbed, as fixest and reghdfe: `fe: firm + year`; `firm:year` for
                interacted effects; singletons are dropped and reported.                                      (shared)
    se:         classical | robust | hc2 | hc3 = classical. Standard-error type; `robust` is HC1, as Stata's
                `robust`; `bootstrap` from 1.1. With sampling weights the default is `robust`, and `se:
                classical` is an error (Z0410). With `weight_type: frequency`, classical errors are valid
                and the observation count is the sum of the weights.                                          (shared)
    level:      Float = 0.95. Confidence level. Confidence level for `ci` and the printed table.              (shared)

VALUE
    A `RegFit`.

DETAILS
    Tall-skinny Householder QR.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    W1001   near-singular design, with the condition number

ACCURACY
    Closed form: within 1e-6 relative of R 4.4 lm.

REFERENCES
    Davidson & MacKinnon (2004), Econometric Theory and Methods, chapters 3 and 5.

SEE ALSO
    ivreg, report

EXAMPLES
    > wages.reg(lwage ~ educ)
    ...
